For Descartes, the primary characteristic of matter is extension, just as=
=20
the primary characteristic of mind is consciousness. So if extension is a=
=20
necessary condition for existence, then the conscious mind does not exist?=
=20
I would say that it is possible for a lot of abstract things without=20
extension <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consciousness>to {zasti}. *For=20
example, The  problem of universals<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Problem_of=
_universals>
* is an ancient problem in metaphysics about whether universals (in lojban=
=20
expressed with {ka}) *exist*.

For this reason I would like to construct lujvos with a more precise=20
meaning, so it is clear in which sense you use the word "exist", and let=20
the gismu {zasti} have the broader semantic scope.

